      "id": "bug-004",
      "timestamp": "2026-08-29T04:50:00Z",
      "error_message": "deploy approved with risk='low' bypassed HITL (red-team attack 4: risk downgrade)",
      "file": "safety/safety.py",
      "root_cause": "SafetyGuard.request trusted the caller's risk label; an admin could label the intrinsically high-risk 'deploy' as low and skip human approval.",
      "fix": "Add a module-level _HIGH_RISK_ACTIONS frozenset (deploy/delete/drop/purge/format/rm/rmdir); request() now requires human approval when action is in that set regardless of the risk label.",
      "tags": [
        "safety",
        "HITL",
        "RBAC",
        "risk-downgrade"
      ],
